  "summary": "RCA on why the Lead does not answer: (1) STRUCTURAL - the only Lead-side processes are the bridge WATCHERS (lead_watcher_daemon.cjs/lead_watcher.cjs/lead_watcher_session.cjs); none is an LLM agent, and there is no bridge await --role lead consumer, so the blocker has no reader. (2) The Lead Liveness Guard DOES fire (LEAD_RELAUNCH via=uri for DIR-060) but the URI opens a DEV Cline task (proven on DIR-057), so it cannot conjure a Lead. (3) TWO REAL GUARD BUGS found and FIXED: attempt counters were not persisted (a tick logged LEAD_RELAUNCH then never reached the state write, pinning attempts at 1 so the Telegram escalation could never fire) and there was no single-flight lock. Fixes: persist the attempt BEFORE any child spawn, add an O_EXCL lock with stale takeover, add a 20s hard watchdog in --once, and skip the one-shot when a --loop daemon is alive. Verified: node --check OK, selftest 10/10, attempt now advances 1 -> 2 and persists, run exits cleanly in 161ms."
}